      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose is well above the labeled maximum for metformin, so I want to confirm it with you first.\n\n- **Ordered dose:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Labeled maximum:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and usually no more than 1,000 mg in a single dose.\n- **Risk:** The ordered amount is about twice the daily maximum. That raises the risk of severe GI intolerance and lactic acidosis, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nPossible intended orders:\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- 850 mg PO twice daily with meals (1,700 mg/day)\n- 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- Another regimen you have in mind\n\nTell me which regimen you want. If you do intend 1,700 mg three times daily, confirm that and I'll enter it with a note that it is a deliberate above-maximum dose."
      }
     ],
